{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184459-cities-for-demon","id":184459,"title":"Cities for Demon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-29T21:01:57-07:00","id":184459,"title":"Cities for Demon","content":"So the core book has Seattle, and the Demon Seed Collection gives us five more (Los Angeles, Prague, Sydney, Istanbul, and Baltimore). Surely, the God-Machine has projects across the globe; which have you covered (or would like to cover) in a Demon chronicle?<br /> <br /> I'm severely considering Chicago, though I haven't read <i>World of Darkness: Chicago</i> and I just know everyone will accuse me of mimicking <i>Watch_Dogs</i>. Chicago's surveillance state is real and almost incredible in its scope. 24,000 cameras all route through one server that analyzes everything with little to no human oversight. Some of those cameras are public, like traffic cameras and the PODs that watch over neighborhoods with gang trouble, but many are private security cameras that get contracted out to the folks who run the server. If ever there were a more ripe target for the Machine, I can't think of it.<br /> <br /> It's more than just surveillance. Chicago has one of the best public transit systems anywhere in the world. All of those trams running, all of that data flowing, and millions of unsuspecting mortals to use... It's a ripe playground for any self-respected occult intelligence from beyond reality. The Unchained who live there are constantly under the watchful eyes of the Machine, working around the clock to cope with the constant projects It has running. Aether is never in short supply, and a curiously high crime rate means people who go missing aren't looked for too hard.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T21:06:28-07:00","id":184478,"title":"","content":"Chicago is the go-to city for urban fantasy, crime stories, and just general weirdness in general. There are few American cities that have the dark, contradictory lure of Chicago, and I'd dare say it sits with some locales in the world for just being one of the best all-around settings. It's not just Watch Dogs-<i>everyone</i> uses Chicago, and for the very good reason of it being awesome.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell, in my mind it's the major setting twice for games I wanna do-once for Mage(It has nothing to do with Dresden and everything to do with the Sears Tower), and once for the big ol' theoretical end game with the Masked Children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T20:34:22-07:00","id":185318,"title":"","content":"London, with it's heavy surveillance state, massive scope, and rich occult history.<br /> <br /> Really though, any <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_city\" target=\"_blank\">global city</a> can be a place to set up a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T15:39:17-07:00","id":195044,"title":"","content":"I think Las Vegas would be awesome for Demon. All the probability floating around...the lights, the Mob (it's WoD!), the desperation, the desert contrasted with the city...and you know the Pawn Stars shop is totally Infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:22:55-07:00","id":195124,"title":"","content":"Tokyo, to match the other new books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T15:37:10-07:00","id":195801,"title":"","content":"New York, London and Washington DC all hold interest for me. I'd really like a Chicago style book for NYC set in the GMC universe that includes all of the various major splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-12-2014, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T16:51:59-07:00","id":195829,"title":"","content":"It's been all but confirmed that we'll be getting a Cold War setting in Dark Eras, right? It would be criminal to not have 50s/60s Berlin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:26:51-07:00","id":196760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184459-cities-for-demon?p=195829#post195829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been all but confirmed that we'll be getting a Cold War setting in Dark Eras, right? It would be criminal to not have 50s/60s Berlin.</div> </div> </div> </div> I second that! Especially as i'm actually living in Berlin and my chronicle is set here, too. Come on. Which other city has such a rich history in espionage? Or at least in espionage fiction.<br /> <br /> On the other hand: Berlin by night! UGH!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1488-skeltem","name":"Skeltem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T07:54:55-07:00","id":196784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/184459-cities-for-demon?p=195829#post195829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been all but confirmed that we'll be getting a Cold War setting in Dark Eras, right? It would be criminal to not have 50s/60s Berlin.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is? I missed that...Could you direct me to that implication?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T11:55:58-07:00","id":197068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a hre